<%# App-wide flash region. The auth screens rely on this being here: the log-in
    view (devise/sessions/new) carries NO error summary on purpose because "Devise
    answers a bad login with a flash", and invisible_captcha's spam responses
    communicate only through flash too. Without this partial every such message was
    invisible and a blocked/failed submit looked like a dead button.

    `flash` in a view includes `flash.now` values for the current render, so this
    catches both the redirect case (a successful "Signed in" notice) and the inline
    re-render case (Devise's `flash.now[:alert]` on a bad login).

    The whole region — container included — renders ONLY when there is a non-blank
    message, so it adds no vertical footprint to the (overwhelming majority of)
    pages that carry no flash.

    Colour: this is NOT the red validation panel. Red is reserved to
    devise/shared/_error_messages ("the only place red appears in Hoojah"), so the
    banner uses the neutral `card-2`/`ink` surface tokens with a `primary` left
    accent — visible, on-palette, and it introduces no new colour.

    `data-turbo-temporary` so Turbo discards the banner on the next visit and a
    stale message never outlives the request that produced it. %>
<% messages = flash.to_h.reject { |_type, message| message.blank? } %>
<% if messages.any? %>
  <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-6 pt-4">
    <% messages.each do |type, message| %>
      <div data-turbo-temporary
           class="mb-4 rounded bg-card-2 text-ink text-sm px-3 py-2 border-l-4 border-primary"
           data-flash="<%= type %>" role="<%= type.to_s == "alert" ? "alert" : "status" %>">
        <%= message %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
<% end %>
